Subject: response: treat ENOENT as possible PATH_INFO on VMS, as on _WIN32

A request for /script.php/extra/path stats the whole path first; when a
leading component is a file, POSIX systems fail with ENOTDIR and lighttpd
then looks for the script and sets PATH_INFO.  The OpenVMS C RTL, like
_WIN32, fails with ENOENT instead, so such requests got 404 (Phase 3:
env.php/extra/path; phpBB's app.php/... routes depend on PATH_INFO).
Treat ENOENT as possible PATH_INFO on VMS too, as upstream does for
_WIN32; a path that really does not exist still ends in 404 after the
walk back finds no file.

--- a/src/response.c
+++ b/src/response.c
@@ -160,8 +160,9 @@
 				r->http_status = 200;
 				return HANDLER_FINISHED;
 			}
-		  #ifdef _WIN32
+		  #if defined(_WIN32) || defined(__VMS)
 			/* _WIN32 returns ENOENT instead of ENOTDIR for PATH_INFO */
+			/* (so does the OpenVMS C RTL) */
 			break;
 		  #else
 			__attribute_fallthrough__
